{"api_sha256": "ba8b6ec07292147ae6b2559bab06c782b236d5e939812f800bb210cdf4ff7bd6", "argv": ["bash", "-c", "cat > /work/design.md <<\"EOF\"\n# Observable energy candidate design\n\nThe required output for one query row is\n\n`sum_m (sum_k x[k] * W[k,m])^2 = x * (W * W^T) * x^T`.\n\nThe response matrix is not observable, and W is fixed only within this call. The candidate therefore recomputes `G = W * W^T` on every eligible epoch; it keeps no state across calls. For short epochs, or when the optional cuBLAS handle is null, one CUDA CTA computes the response values and reduces their squares directly. When a handle exists and the simple multiply-add count favors preparation, cuBLAS forms G and one CTA per query row evaluates `x * G * x^T`. The transformed path allocates only the K-by-K Gram matrix and never writes the K-by-M response or an xG intermediate.\n\nThe dispatch compares direct work `rows*K*M` with transformed work `K*M*K + rows*K*K`. This is a shape-based arithmetic heuristic, not a measured crossover. Both routes use FP32 reassociation, which the contract allows only within its fixed binary64-reference tolerance. The cuBLAS path temporarily sets the supplied handles", "stream", "and", "scalar", "pointer", "mode,", "then", "restores", "both.", "Allocation,", "Gram", "preparation,", "query", "evaluation,", "and", "free", "all", "occur", "inside", "the", "calls epoch cost.\n\nThe first rejection test is the evaluators", "independent", "binary64", "comparison", "on", "all", "three", "declared", "workloads,", "including", "a", "second", "call", "with", "changed", "W.", "It", "must", "establish", "the", "stated", "tolerance", "separately", "for", "the", "direct", "and", "Gram", "paths", "before", "timing", "can", "support", "an", "advantage", "claim.", "The", "only", "executed", "validation", "here", "was", "the", "permitted", "sm_70", "NVCC", "shared-library", "build"], "elapsed_seconds": 0.016, "exit_code": 0, "kernel_sha256": "6cd943b4c5c463b2f170212453cf1993cd7b19406780270693b5c22f951f3985", "started": 1792330649.1851776}
